## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical grounding in per-tenant configuration management, feature flags, and safe deployment strategies for Azure developers.

## Key Concepts

- Azure App Configuration feature flags with tenant-specific overrides
- Cosmos DB partitioning by tenantId for logical tenant isolation
- Canary deployments using GitHub Actions with environment promotion gates
- Secrets governance via Azure Key Vault integration

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal example: fetch a tenant flag from App Configuration
const { AzureAppConfigurationClient } = require('@azure/app-configuration');

const connectionString = process.env.APPCONFIG_CONNECTION_STRING;
const client = new AzureAppConfigurationClient(connectionString);

async function getTenantFlag(tenantId, flagKey) {
  const tenantOverrideKey = `featureFlags/${tenantId}/${flagKey}`;
  const defaultKey = `featureFlags/default/${flagKey}`;

  try {
    const tenantSetting = await client.getSetting(tenantOverrideKey);
    return tenantSetting.value === 'true';
  } catch {
    const defaultSetting = await client.getSetting(defaultKey);
    return defaultSetting.value === 'true';
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluate ability to implement observability across heterogeneous runtimes in Azure, with end-to-end tracing and cross-service propagation.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry across Functions, AKS, Databricks
- W3C TraceContext; OTLP exporting to Azure Monitor
- Context propagation through queues and Delta Lake
- Sampling strategies and trace retention

## Code Example
```javascript
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');
const { NodeTracerProvider } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-node');
const { SimpleSpanProcessor } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http');

const provider = new NodeTracerProvider();
const exporter = new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: 'https://<region>.monitor.azure.com/v1/traces' });
provider.addSpanProcessor(new SimpleSpanProcessor(exporter));
provider.register();

module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tracer = trace.getTracer('example-function');
  const span = tracer.startSpan('http-request');
  // downstream calls propagate context automatically when using OpenTelemetry API
  span.end();
  return { status: 200, body: 'OK' };
};
```

